// stdlib/ugraph.sa -- extended grapheme clusters (Unicode UAX #29).
//
// Dependencies: import stdlib/utf8.sa and stdlib/uwidth.sa BEFORE this module.
// Like money.sa over decimal.sa, this module names its dependencies' functions
// without importing them, because the module loader does not dedupe a diamond
// and a second import would declare those functions twice.
//
// Why this exists. stdlib/utext.sa counts code points, which is the right unit
// for storage but the wrong unit for a reader: "e" plus U+0301 is two code
// points and one visible character, a Hangul syllable can be three Jamo, a
// family emoji is several emoji joined by ZWJ, and a flag is two regional
// indicators. This module implements the standard clustering rules so text can
// be counted, sliced and reversed a character at a time.
//
// The rules implemented are GB1-GB999 of UAX #29 including the Unicode 15.1
// Indic conjunct break rules (GB9c, via the InCB property) and the emoji ZWJ
// rule (GB11). Concretely, a break is refused between:
//
//   GB3    CR and LF
//   GB4/5  nothing joins to or from Control, CR or LF (except GB3)
//   GB6-8  the Hangul syllable sequences L x (L|V|LV|LVT), (LV|V) x (V|T),
//          (LVT|T) x T; LV and LVT are computed from the syllable block rather
//          than tabulated
//   GB9    anything and Extend or ZWJ
//   GB9a   anything and SpacingMark
//   GB9b   Prepend and anything
//   GB9c   an Indic conjunct: Consonant [Extend Linker]* Linker [Extend Linker]*
//          and a following Consonant
//   GB11   Extended_Pictographic Extend* ZWJ and Extended_Pictographic
//   GB12/13 two regional indicators, but only in pairs, so a run of four
//          indicators is two flags and a run of three is a flag plus one
//   GB999  everywhere else
//
// Failure contract: malformed or over-long text gives -1 from counts and "" from
// text, exactly like stdlib/utext.sa. ug_count("") is 0 and valid.
//
// The tables below are generated; see the marker comment. They come from the
// Unicode 17.0.0 Character Database files themselves (GraphemeBreakProperty.txt,
// emoji/emoji-data.txt and DerivedCoreProperties.txt for InCB), the same single
// source as stdlib/uwidth.sa, compressed to inclusive ranges and searched by
// bisection.
//
// Verification: selfhost/stdlib_ugraph_test.sa runs all 766 cases of the official
// Unicode 17.0.0 GraphemeBreakTest.txt conformance file, sweeps the class,
// Extended_Pictographic and InCB lookups over all 1114112 code points, and checks
// the cluster API against an independent rule-regex reference.

// Grapheme_Cluster_Break classes. Other is 0 so an untabulated scalar is Other.
make ug_cls_other() -> num {
  give 0
}
make ug_cls_control() -> num {
  give 1
}
make ug_cls_cr() -> num {
  give 2
}
make ug_cls_lf() -> num {
  give 3
}
make ug_cls_extend() -> num {
  give 4
}
make ug_cls_zwj() -> num {
  give 5
}
make ug_cls_ri() -> num {
  give 6
}
make ug_cls_l() -> num {
  give 7
}
make ug_cls_v() -> num {
  give 8
}
make ug_cls_t() -> num {
  give 9
}
make ug_cls_lv() -> num {
  give 10
}
make ug_cls_lvt() -> num {
  give 11
}
make ug_cls_prepend() -> num {
  give 12
}
make ug_cls_spacing() -> num {
  give 13
}

